  "strategy": "2. **Approach and Rationale**\n\n   Central Idea:\n   This approach applies multi-resolution optimization using spatial basis functions (Gaussian bumps) with adaptive dimension reduction and optimization strategies. The core idea is to represent the piecewise constant function first using a flexible number of basis functions (Gaussian bumps) placed optimally, which:\n\n   - Captures non-local dependencies in the overlap minimization task\n   - Exploits relative strengths of continuous- and combinatorial-based optimizers\n   - Enables progressive dimension refinement and parallelable grid resolutions\n\n   The main bottleneck addressed is premature convergence in local optima due to rigid grid projection. By using a weighted-sum representation with learnable basis functions and sequentially reducing the effective grid dimension while maintaining solution quality, we directly control resolution and storage.\n\n   Important Limitations:\n   - Grid-based final translation may introduce discretization artifacts\n   - Basis function placement may cluster or miss boundary features\n   - No explicit basis sparsity promotion in initial configuration\n\n   These limitations are justified by the need for balance between diversity preservation and optimization tractability.\n\n3. **Mathematical Specification**\n\n   Representation:\n   We represent the piecewise constant function h(x) as a linear combination of normalized Gaussian basis functions on [0,2]:\n\n   h(x) = (1/V) * \u2211_{m=1}^{M} A_m * exp(-(x - \u03bc_m)^2 / (2\u03c3_m^2))\n   \n   Where V = \u222b\u2080^2 h(x) dx, and parameters (A_m, \u03bc_m, \u03c3_m) are nonnegative real numbers. The function is constrained by:\n   - 0 \u2264 h[x] \u2264 1 (transformed via clipping and renormalization)\n   - V = 1 (handled by constraints)\n\n   Objective:\n   C5 = max_{k integer} [dx * (np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')).max()]\n   Where dx = 2/n_points\n\n   Constraints:\n   - Sum(h_i) * dx = 1 (solved by shape constraints)\n   - h(x) \u2208 [0,1]^n_points (handled during transformation from base variables)\n\n   4. **Implementation Procedure**\n\n   main() Sequence:\n   ```\n   [INITIALIZATION] \n   Validate input; initialize parent fallback; set meta_parameters();\n\n   [PHASE 0: Basis Selection]\n   Generate candidate basis structure; select initial M_basis opt configurable;\n\n   [PHASE 1: Weighted Grid Optimization]\n   Steps:\n     - Represent piecewise basis functions with parametric variables\n     - Transform Gaussian placement to grid representation with dx\n     - Apply alternating projection and Poisson optimization\n\n   [PHASE 2: Progressive Resolution Training]\n   Steps:\n     - Start at coarse grid (n=10) verify solution streak\n     - Increase grid resolution via parameter duplication; extend basis counts\n     - Apply alternate gradient & combinatorial optimizations\n\n   [PHASE 3: Spatial Smoothing & Feature Locking]\n   Steps:\n     - Apply spatial Laplacian smoothing to maintain local features\n     - Lock grid dimensions when improvement below threshold\n     - Final refinement\n\n   [PHASE 4: Duplicate Detection & Early Exit]\n   Steps:\n     - Compute fingerprint of current solution\n     - If duplicate detected with improvement >= X%, break and report\n   ```\n\n   5. **Search Choices and Variations**\n\n   Default Settings:\n   - Basis families: Gaussian bumps (default) | Uniform tents (varied)\n   - Initial M_basis = ceil(sqrt(n_points/4))\n   - Basis width scaling = adaptive width minimization rather than fixed\n   - Grid expansion factor = 2 each level (allows pigeonhole tracking)\n   - Optimization schedule: 2-stage: first combinatorial rough optimization, then gradient polishing\n\n   6. **Compute Budget and Robustness**\n\n   Phased Execution:\n   - Phase 0: 10%\n   - Phase 1: 40%\n   - Phase 2: 30%\n   - Phase 3: 20%\n   - Checkpoints at resolution doublings; safe improvements last full checkpoint window\n\n   Fallback Mechanism:\n   - On failure, return best from available parameters\n   - Preserve all parent solutions across resolutions\n   - Re-validate final candidate before return\n\n   Bayesian Optimization Context Window:\n\n   To be added after implementation.",
